ear the village of Petřkovice in the Czech Republic, this artifact belongs to the Upper Paleolithic period, a time when human societies were primarily nomadic hunter-gatherers. Its significance lies not only in its artistic merit but also in what it reveals about the social and cultural practices of early human communities across Europe, particularly in the context of fertility cults and matrifocal societies.

